From 01b748752ee601f94b44c6de93a17f06a08d51a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: idontwannagoo <35237425+idontwannagoo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 19:55:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] options: add secondary-sub-scale

This allows scaling secondary subtitles independently from primary subtitles. The option defaults to 1 like --sub-scale and follows the other secondary-sub-* options by not inheriting from the primary subtitle setting.

Fixes #14989.
---
 DOCS/interface-changes/secondary-sub-scale.txt | 2 ++
 DOCS/man/options.rst                           | 4 ++++
 options/options.c                              | 7 +++++--
 options/options.h                              | 2 +-
 player/command.c                               | 1 +
 sub/sd_ass.c                                   | 3 ++-
 sub/sd_lavc.c                                  | 4 ++--
 7 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 DOCS/interface-changes/secondary-sub-scale.txt

diff --git a/DOCS/interface-changes/secondary-sub-scale.txt b/DOCS/interface-changes/secondary-sub-scale.txt
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..0119db931
--- /dev/null
+++ b/DOCS/interface-changes/secondary-sub-scale.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+add `--secondary-sub-scale` option
+`--sub-scale` now only affects primary subtitles
diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
index 460e12433..105e37b36 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -2518,6 +2518,10 @@ Subtitles
         This affects ASS subtitles as well, and may lead to incorrect subtitle
         rendering. Use with care, or use ``--sub-font-size`` instead.
 
+``--secondary-sub-scale=<0-100>``
+    Factor for the secondary subtitle font size. This is similar to
+    ``--sub-scale`` but for secondary subtitles (default: 1).
+
 ``--sub-scale-signs=<yes|no>``
     When set to yes, also apply ``--sub-scale`` to typesetting (or "signs").
     When this is set to no, ``--sub-scale`` is only applied to dialogue. The
